&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Joblogic Story&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Established in 1998,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic&lt;/strong&gt; is the UK’s #1 &lt;strong&gt;Field Service Management&lt;/strong&gt; (FSM) software platform. We are a global business with offices in the &lt;strong&gt;UK&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Pakistan&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Vietnam&lt;/strong&gt;. Since our management buy-out in 2013, we have grown from &lt;strong&gt;~£500K &lt;/strong&gt;ARR to &lt;strong&gt;~£35M+ &lt;/strong&gt;ARR and expanded our team from 11 to 500+ people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recently, we secured a strategic growth investment from &lt;strong&gt;Vista Equity Partners &lt;/strong&gt;— a global technology investor specialising in enterprise software. This investment includes over &lt;strong&gt;£100&lt;/strong&gt; million in new primary capital and will fuel our next phase of growth by accelerating our &lt;strong&gt;AI-first roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;, expanding our platform into CAFM (Computer-Aided Facilities Management) capabilities, and supporting our expansion across Europe and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With &lt;strong&gt;Vista’s &lt;/strong&gt;backing, we’re transforming from a successful UK business into a global scaling SaaS rocket ship, and we’d love for you to join us on our journey to &lt;strong&gt;£100M &lt;/strong&gt;ARR across international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic &lt;/strong&gt;provides software to service contractors who install and maintain the built environment. Our platform helps businesses streamline operations, improve profitability, ensure compliance, and achieve rapid growth. With over &lt;strong&gt;100,000&lt;/strong&gt; users across industries including HVAC, plumbing, electrical maintenance, facilities management, and building fabric maintenance, we are entering a new era of intelligent automation, predictive maintenance, and data-driven decision-making for service firms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;We’re hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Head of Paid&lt;/strong&gt; to lead our paid acquisition engine, with a clear focus on MQL delivery and ARR impact. Reporting to the Chief Revenue Officer, you will own a paid media budget of £3.6M+ a year. You will be a player-coach: hands-on in the key channels, while coaching two acquisition specialists and getting strong value from our embedded agency. You’ll bring rigour, pace and clarity through data, experimentation and excellent stakeholder management.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be accountable for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary: Marketing Qualified Leads (MQLs)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver MQL volume to plan, with clear definitions, reporting and SLA alignment with Sales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve MQL-to-SQL conversion by raising lead quality and tightening the handover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secondary: ARR impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve contribution to new ARR by optimising for downstream conversion, not just top-of-funnel volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build visibility from channel spend → MQL → SQL → closed-won ARR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Efficiency guardrails&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAC, CPA, CPL and ROAS are not the north star, but you’ll manage them as guardrails while scaling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll actively reduce wasted spend and improve marginal returns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will increase paid acquisition success in bigger businesses. That means:&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;clearer segmentation for higher-value accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;stronger qualification routes into Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;messaging and proof points that resonate with more complex buying groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;channel mix and targeting tuned for higher ACV, longer sales cycles and higher scrutiny&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paid acquisition strategy and execution (hands-on)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the multi-channel strategy and performance across Google Ads and Microsoft Ads, paid social (LinkedIn, Meta), display, YouTube and remarketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Add channels where justified, such as review sites, affiliates and industry partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and allocate a £3.6M+ annual paid media budget, shifting spend based on pipeline and ARR impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build campaign structures that scale cleanly by segment (bigger businesses, priority verticals, intent level), offer (demo, assessment, content, webinars) and funnel stage (prospecting vs retargeting).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimentation and conversion improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a structured experimentation programme across ads (targeting, creative, landing page alignment), landing pages and forms, and lead capture and nurture routes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an experiment log with hypotheses, expected lift, success criteria and learnings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement, attribution and insight (HubSpot + Power BI)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own reporting in HubSpot (tactical, day-to-day) and Power BI (executive reporting, trends, cohort movement), liaising with our Data team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure clean lifecycle tracking and accurate attribution: channel tagging standards, lifecycle stage definitions, data hygiene and campaign-to-MQL reporting integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build forecasts and business cases that leadership can trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership: player-coach and agency management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach two acquisition specialists through weekly performance reviews, skills development plans, and clear ownership boundaries and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage our embedded agency with tight briefs, strong measurement and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a calm, high-output team cadence where priorities, timelines and decisions are explicit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder management and commercial influence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales leadership and SDR/BDR teams to align on MQL definitions and SLAs, improve speed-to-lead and follow-up sequences, and use feedback loops to improve lead quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate budgets and secure investment: present trade-offs, quantify expected impact, and explain risks and assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in performance marketing, paid media or digital acquisition (B2B SaaS strongly preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience owning and allocating annual paid media budgets of £3.6M+, accountable for ROI and marginal returns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of delivering MQL growth at pace while improving conversion to revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on expertise in Google Ads: account structure, query strategy, bidding, audiences and measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong capability in LinkedIn Ads for B2B, plus other paid channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytics and reporting: HubSpot reporting and lifecycle stages, and Power BI fluency (or equivalent, with evidence of decision-grade reporting).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing stakeholders with data, not opinions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to coach and raise the bar for a small team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Traits we’ll hire for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detail-obsessed:&lt;/strong&gt; tracking, naming conventions, data hygiene and QA are second nature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High learning velocity:&lt;/strong&gt; fast, disciplined iteration with clear hypotheses and honest read-outs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial judgement:&lt;/strong&gt; you know when to chase volume and when to protect quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calm leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; you make the team better and bring the business with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong communication:&lt;/strong&gt; crisp updates, clear decisions, no noise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shifting upmarket (bigger businesses, higher ACV, longer cycles).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRO expertise (landing pages, forms, onsite journeys).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with working alongside an SDR motion and sequencing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with review sites and intent-based channels in B2B software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high-ownership role with a significant budget and direct access to the Marketing team, Rev Ops team and Data/Business Intelligence team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong tools: HubSpot and Power BI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A business that values data, clarity and accountable growth, with Vista Equity Partners behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working: 2 days in our Birmingham office, 3 from home.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Birmingham, England (hybrid: 2 days in the office, 3 days working from home)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; Chief Revenue Officer&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Visa sponsorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Not available for this role. Applicants must have the right to work in the UK.&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Joblogic Story&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
