&lt;p&gt;Established in 1998,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic&lt;/strong&gt; is the UK’s #1 &lt;strong&gt;Field Service Management&lt;/strong&gt; (FSM) software platform. We are a global business with offices in the &lt;strong&gt;UK&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Pakistan&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Vietnam&lt;/strong&gt;. Since our management buy-out in 2013, we have grown from &lt;strong&gt;~£500K &lt;/strong&gt;ARR to &lt;strong&gt;~£35M+ &lt;/strong&gt;ARR and expanded our team from 11 to 500+ people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recently, we secured a strategic growth investment from &lt;strong&gt;Vista Equity Partners &lt;/strong&gt;— a global technology investor specialising in enterprise software. This investment includes over &lt;strong&gt;£100&lt;/strong&gt; million in new primary capital and will fuel our next phase of growth by accelerating our &lt;strong&gt;AI-first roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;, expanding our platform into CAFM (Computer-Aided Facilities Management) capabilities, and supporting our expansion across Europe and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With &lt;strong&gt;Vista’s &lt;/strong&gt;backing, we’re transforming from a successful UK business into a global scaling SaaS rocket ship, and we’d love for you to join us on our journey to &lt;strong&gt;£100M &lt;/strong&gt;ARR across international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic &lt;/strong&gt;provides software to service contractors who install and maintain the built environment. Our platform helps businesses streamline operations, improve profitability, ensure compliance, and achieve rapid growth. With over &lt;strong&gt;100,000&lt;/strong&gt; users across industries including HVAC, plumbing, electrical maintenance, facilities management, and building fabric maintenance, we are entering a new era of intelligent automation, predictive maintenance, and data-driven decision-making for service firms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Objective:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To act as the first point of contact for emergency calls relating to building operations across the UK outside of business hours. The role ensures urgent issues are triaged, logged, and resolved efficiently by dispatching the correct personnel, keeping stakeholders updated, and maintaining high levels of customer service&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Duties:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Answer and log incoming emergency calls (e.g., leaks, electrical faults, heating/cooling failures, fire alarms, access issues).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use clear questioning and listening skills to triage calls, establish urgency, and escalate where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dispatch jobs to engineers, contractors, or emergency responders and monitor progress to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep customers and stakeholders informed with timely updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately record all call details and updates within the service management system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple issues simultaneously, making sound decisions under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure complete and accurate handovers between shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow health, safety, and compliance procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Always deliver a high standard of professionalism, empathy, and reassurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator with a professional telephone manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calm and logical in emergency situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and decision-making skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to multitask and prioritise effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail with accurate recording of information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using IT systems, databases, and email.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible and willing to work irregular hours, including nights and weekends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a helpdesk, call centre, or facilities management environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of building systems (electrical, plumbing, fire alarms, access control).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in emergency response or triage-type roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hours &amp;amp; place of Work &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote (UK-based), with initial in-office training as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;Shift pattern: 4 days on / 2 days off,&lt;strong&gt; 5&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;pm- 1am or 1am to 9am&lt;/strong&gt;, including weekends and Bank holidays&lt;/h5&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Joblogic Story&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Established in 1998,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic&lt;/strong&gt; is the UK’s #1 &lt;strong&gt;Field Service Management&lt;/strong&gt; (FSM) software platform. We are a global business with offices in the &lt;strong&gt;UK&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Pakistan&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Vietnam&lt;/strong&gt;. Since our management buy-out in 2013, we have grown from &lt;strong&gt;~£500K &lt;/strong&gt;ARR to &lt;strong&gt;~£35M+ &lt;/strong&gt;ARR and expanded our team from 11 to 500+ people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recently, we secured a strategic growth investment from &lt;strong&gt;Vista Equity Partners &lt;/strong&gt;— a global technology investor specialising in enterprise software. This investment includes over &lt;strong&gt;£100&lt;/strong&gt; million in new primary capital and will fuel our next phase of growth by accelerating our &lt;strong&gt;AI-first roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;, expanding our platform into CAFM (Computer-Aided Facilities Management) capabilities, and supporting our expansion across Europe and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With &lt;strong&gt;Vista’s &lt;/strong&gt;backing, we’re transforming from a successful UK business into a global scaling SaaS rocket ship, and we’d love for you to join us on our journey to &lt;strong&gt;£100M &lt;/strong&gt;ARR across international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic &lt;/strong&gt;provides software to service contractors who install and maintain the built environment. Our platform helps businesses streamline operations, improve profitability, ensure compliance, and achieve rapid growth. With over &lt;strong&gt;100,000&lt;/strong&gt; users across industries including HVAC, plumbing, electrical maintenance, facilities management, and building fabric maintenance, we are entering a new era of intelligent automation, predictive maintenance, and data-driven decision-making for service firms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You’ll own three go-to-market motions: Referral &amp;amp; Reseller (channel pipeline and ARR), Technology (ISV and integration partnerships), and Market Expansion (G-Cloud, procurement frameworks, analyst relations). You’ll report directly into the CRO, work across Sales, Marketing, and Product, and operate across Joblogic Core (FSM), Invida (CAFM), and our acquired brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;This is a revenue-owning role. You’ll carry a partner-sourced ARR target from Q2 with a ramp in place.&amp;nbsp;If you want to manage a programme someone else built, this isn’t it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Build the partnerships function&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Design Joblogic’s partner programme from scratch — commercial framework, partner tiers,activation criteria, and go-to-market motions&lt;br&gt;• Create the commercial infrastructure: partner agreement templates, deal registration, MDF&amp;nbsp;budget framework&lt;br&gt;• Define what a good partner looks like and what activation means in practice&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Referral &amp;amp; Reseller&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Identify, approach, and sign referral and reseller partners with genuine pipeline potential&lt;br&gt;• Own the partner-sourced ARR number — not pipeline created, not partners signed, closed ARR&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;•Manage the full partner lifecycle including offboarding underperformers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Technology Partnerships&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Build ISV and integration partnerships that extend Joblogic’s value proposition&lt;br&gt;• Work with Product and Engineering to define how technology partnership requests get&amp;nbsp;evaluated and prioritised&lt;br&gt;• Identify integration opportunities that reduce churn and increase stickiness&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Market Expansion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Explore and pursue G-Cloud and procurement framework routes to market&lt;br&gt;• Build relationships with relevant analyst communities&lt;br&gt;• Identify channel opportunities in adjacent markets and buyer communities&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Internal alignment and co-sell&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Establish and hold Sales to a co-sell SLA — partner leads followed up within agreed&amp;nbsp;timeframes&lt;br&gt;• Build visibility of partner-sourced pipeline in HubSpot so attribution is clean from day one&lt;br&gt;• Operate with influence, not authority — Sales, Marketing, and Product are stakeholders, not&amp;nbsp;reports&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Exec and board reporting&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Report partner-sourced ARR, activation rates, and programme health to the CRO&lt;br&gt;• Frame partnership value in commercial terms — revenue, coverage, strategic fit — not&amp;nbsp;relationship health scores&lt;br&gt;• Present at exec and board level as the programme matures&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Be Measured:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Partner-sourced closed ARR against quarterly target&lt;br&gt;• Partner activation rate — signed partners generating pipeline vs. total signed&lt;br&gt;• Deal registration pipeline volume and conversion&lt;br&gt;• Number of partners signed and activated within 90 days&lt;br&gt;• Co-sell SLA adherence with Sales&lt;br&gt;• Programme milestones: commercial framework live, HubSpot attribution active, MDF&amp;nbsp;structure agreed&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-have&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• You have built or led a partnerships function — not just contributed to one&lt;br&gt;• You have personally signed commercial partner agreements and managed them through to&amp;nbsp;activation&lt;br&gt;• You can evidence a pipeline or ARR contribution you have personally owned and reported on&lt;br&gt;• You have managed the full partner lifecycle including offboarding underperformers&lt;br&gt;• Active HubSpot user who manages and reports partner pipeline in the CRM&lt;br&gt;• You understand co-sell mechanics operationally — not just conceptually&lt;br&gt;• You use AI tools daily and can describe specifically what you’ve built or automated with them&lt;br&gt;• Experience in a PE-backed or high-growth SaaS environment&lt;br&gt;• Comfortable with ambiguity, quarterly accountability, and building without mature&amp;nbsp;infrastructure&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strongly preferred&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Background in UK SaaS businesses at £10M–£60M ARR — close enough to our stage to have&amp;nbsp;relevant scar tissue&lt;br&gt;• Experience with deal registration and MDF budget management&lt;br&gt;• G-Cloud or procurement framework experience&lt;br&gt;• Familiarity with FSM, CAFM, trades, or SME vertical SaaS — Xero, Sage, COINS, or similar&amp;nbsp;buyer profiles&lt;br&gt;• Former AE or Account Manager who moved into partnerships — strong commercial instincts&amp;nbsp;and CRM discipline&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Ownership language — you say “I built”, “I signed”, “I owned the number”, not “we supported&amp;nbsp;the programme”&lt;br&gt;• Commercial framing — you measure yourself in ARR and pipeline, not meetings held or&amp;nbsp;partners signed&lt;br&gt;• Builder mentality — you’re energised by building from scratch, not managing a mature&amp;nbsp;programme&lt;br&gt;• Operational AI use — you’ve built workflows or automations, not just experimented&lt;br&gt;• Influence without authority — you know how to hold internal teams accountable without a&amp;nbsp;reporting line&lt;br&gt;• PE environment fit — you understand quarterly cadence, investor-grade reporting, and what &#39;good’ looks like at a Vista-backed business&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic Values&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Respect —&lt;/strong&gt; We treat colleagues, partners, and customers with professionalism and empathy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Obsession with Customers —&lt;/strong&gt; We focus on solving real operational problems and delivering&amp;nbsp;meaningful value.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accountability —&lt;/strong&gt; We take ownership of outcomes and hold ourselves to high standards.&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rethink Tomorrow — &lt;/strong&gt;We embrace innovation and continuously improve.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why This Role Matters:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Joblogic has commercial relationships. It doesn’t have a commercial partner programme. With ARR&amp;nbsp;growth targets that require multiple pipeline sources, partner-sourced revenue is an identified gap in&amp;nbsp;our GTM architecture.&lt;br&gt;The CRO joins in July 2026 and is building the commercial function from arrival. This hire is part of the&amp;nbsp;founding commercial layer. You will define how Joblogic generates revenue through partners, shape&amp;nbsp;the go-to-market architecture, and do it with the backing of a PE-funded SaaS business on the path to&amp;nbsp;becoming one of the UK’s fastest growing software companies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Joblogic Story&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Established in 1998,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic&lt;/strong&gt; is the UK’s #1 &lt;strong&gt;Field Service Management&lt;/strong&gt; (FSM) software platform. We are a global business with offices in the &lt;strong&gt;UK&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Pakistan&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Vietnam&lt;/strong&gt;. Since our management buy-out in 2013, we have grown from &lt;strong&gt;~£500K &lt;/strong&gt;ARR to &lt;strong&gt;~£35M+ &lt;/strong&gt;ARR and expanded our team from 11 to 500+ people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recently, we secured a strategic growth investment from &lt;strong&gt;Vista Equity Partners &lt;/strong&gt;— a global technology investor specialising in enterprise software. This investment includes over &lt;strong&gt;£100&lt;/strong&gt; million in new primary capital and will fuel our next phase of growth by accelerating our &lt;strong&gt;AI-first roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;, expanding our platform into CAFM (Computer-Aided Facilities Management) capabilities, and supporting our expansion across Europe and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With &lt;strong&gt;Vista’s &lt;/strong&gt;backing, we’re transforming from a successful UK business into a global scaling SaaS rocket ship, and we’d love for you to join us on our journey to &lt;strong&gt;£100M &lt;/strong&gt;ARR across international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic &lt;/strong&gt;provides software to service contractors who install and maintain the built environment. Our platform helps businesses streamline operations, improve profitability, ensure compliance, and achieve rapid growth. With over &lt;strong&gt;100,000&lt;/strong&gt; users across industries including HVAC, plumbing, electrical maintenance, facilities management, and building fabric maintenance, we are entering a new era of intelligent automation, predictive maintenance, and data-driven decision-making for service firms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Product Director &lt;/strong&gt;to lead the strategy, vision, and execution of Joblogic&#39;s product portfolio across Field Service and Facilities Management. This is a senior leadership role for someone with &lt;strong&gt;broad product expertise, deep domain understanding, strong people leadership and mentoring skills, and a proven ability to design, build, and scale AI-powered products&lt;/strong&gt; in B2B SaaS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own the product vision and roadmap across our entire FSM and CAFM platform, lead, grow, and mentor a high-performing product team, and partner with the executive team to translate market opportunity into commercial outcomes. You&#39;ll also be the driving force behind our AI-first product agenda — defining where AI delivers genuine value, embedding intelligence into core workflows, and ensuring we ship responsibly and at pace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Above all, this is a people leadership role. You&#39;ll be the coach, mentor, and standard-setter for the product team — building careers, raising the craft bar, and creating the kind of environment where ambitious product people do their best work. You&#39;ll be equal parts strategist, people leader, and product craftsperson.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead product across the Joblogic platform, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end FSM and CAFM platform strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-first product initiatives — copilots, agents, predictive maintenance, intelligent scheduling, document intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reactive, PPM, and contract workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scheduling, dispatch, and optimisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Field engineer mobile experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Asset lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quoting → job → invoicing flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer portals and self-service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data, reporting, analytics, and embedded BI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vertical-specific FM workflows (HVAC, M&amp;amp;E, FM, building maintenance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform, integrations, and developer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;1. Set Product Vision &amp;amp; Strategy&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and communicate a compelling 1–3 year product vision aligned to Joblogic&#39;s £100M ARR ambition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate market trends, customer insight, and competitive dynamics into a clear, prioritised portfolio roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sharp build / buy / partner / sunset decisions across the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the CEO, CPO, CTO, CRO, and CCO to align product strategy with commercial and GTM strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;2. Lead the AI-First Product Agenda&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Joblogic&#39;s AI product strategy across LLMs, ML, agents, and predictive analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify the highest-value AI use cases across FSM and CAFM workflows — from intelligent scheduling and dynamic dispatch to predictive maintenance, automated quoting, and engineer copilots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set principles for responsible, safe, and explainable AI — including data, privacy, evaluation, and human-in-the-loop design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to the rapidly evolving AI landscape (foundation models, agentic patterns, RAG, fine-tuning, evals) and translate it into pragmatic product bets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and data leadership to shape the AI platform, data architecture, and ML lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;3. Mentor, Coach &amp;amp; Lead a High-Performing Product Team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, mentor, and develop Product Managers, Senior PMs, and Group PMs across the portfolio — making people growth a core part of how you spend your week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run regular 1:1s, career conversations, and development plans tailored to each PM&#39;s strengths, goals, and growth areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach PMs through complex trade-offs, stakeholder management, difficult prioritisation calls, and high-stakes customer situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the standard for discovery, product craft, written communication, and commercial thinking — and actively raise the bar through feedback and pairing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear team structure, ownership, levelling, and career paths as the function scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong performance culture: clear expectations, candid feedback, recognition, and the courage to make hard people decisions when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a psychologically safe, inclusive environment where customer obsession, evidence-led decisions, and outcome ownership thrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invest in the team&#39;s craft — running PRD reviews, discovery clinics, AI literacy sessions, and post-mortems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;4. Drive Discovery &amp;amp; Customer Insight at Scale&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed deep, continuous discovery across the product team — customer calls, field visits, usage analytics, and qualitative research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a strong personal connection to customers, engineers, planners, and contract managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesise insight across verticals to identify portfolio-level opportunities and risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion design partner programs and beta cohorts for new AI and platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;5. Partner With UX, Engineering &amp;amp; Data&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hand-in-hand with Design and Engineering leadership to ship simple, scalable, beautifully crafted products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set quality bars for usability, performance, reliability, and AI behaviour.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure mobile and web experiences feel like one cohesive, modern product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a strong data and experimentation culture — from instrumentation to A/B testing to outcome reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;6. Own Commercial &amp;amp; Outcome Accountability&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product-led inputs to ARR growth, retention, expansion, and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track product KPIs and OKRs at portfolio and team level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, CS, and Marketing on positioning, packaging, pricing, and launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent product externally — with customers, partners, analysts, investors, and at industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;7. Shape the Operating Model&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how product, design, and engineering work together — rituals, planning cadence, roadmap reviews, discovery operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale the function from a single-product mindset to a multi-product, platform-led operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve roadmap transparency, prioritisation frameworks, and cross-team dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Must-Have (Non-Negotiable)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extensive, proven experience in product management, including substantial experience directly managing and mentoring product managers&lt;/strong&gt; in B2B SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven &lt;strong&gt;people leadership and mentoring track record&lt;/strong&gt; — you&#39;ve built teams from the ground up, developed PMs into Senior PMs and beyond, and can point to specific people whose careers you&#39;ve helped shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of shipping and scaling &lt;strong&gt;AI-powered products&lt;/strong&gt; — from problem framing through to production, evaluation, and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on understanding of &lt;strong&gt;modern AI/ML and GenAI capabilities&lt;/strong&gt;: LLMs, agents, RAG, evals, prompt and context engineering, model selection, fine-tuning, and ML lifecycle trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad product expertise across multiple domains — workflows, platform, mobile, data, integrations — and the ability to set strategy across all of them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Field Service Management, Facilities Management, CAFM/CMMS, Construction Tech, or an adjacent vertical SaaS domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial instinct: comfortable owning revenue-impacting decisions, pricing, packaging, and ROI cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success building, hiring, retaining, and growing product teams of 5–20+ people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent strategic communication — able to translate complex problems into clear narratives for the board, customers, and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;People Leadership &amp;amp; Mentoring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural mentor — you genuinely enjoy growing other people and take pride in their wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at giving direct, kind, actionable feedback — and equally skilled at receiving it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable having hard conversations: performance, levelling, role changes, and tough prioritisation calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong emotional intelligence — you read teams well, spot burnout early, and create space for people to do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of hiring exceptional product talent and building diverse, inclusive teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to flex coaching style — from new PMs needing structure to senior PMs needing sounding-board sparring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Product &amp;amp; Leadership Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product craft: discovery, prioritisation, written specs, systems thinking, and outcome orientation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate at multiple altitudes — from 3-year strategy to specific PRDs and AI evaluation criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating ambiguity, complex stakeholders, and competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data- and evidence-led decision making, balanced with strong product intuition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence without authority across executive, commercial, and technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling product in a PE-backed or high-growth SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to international expansion (Europe, North America).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in scheduling, optimisation, IoT, or operations research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching agentic or copilot experiences in B2B workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APIs, marketplaces, and partner ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering, data science, or design background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why This Role Matters&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joblogic is evolving from a traditional FSM tool into an AI-first, workflow-intelligent, vertical-focused platform — and the Product Director is the single most important hire in shaping that future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;ll directly influence:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How 100,000+ users experience Joblogic every day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where and how AI shows up across the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How quickly we expand into CAFM and international markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The product culture, craft, and bar for the next 100 hires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our path from £25M to £100M ARR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to lead product at a scale where strategy, AI, and execution all matter — and where your decisions show up in the working day of thousands of engineers, planners, and service teams — this is the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Joblogic Values&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Joblogic, we expect our team members to champion and embed our core values across their work and customer interactions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respect – We value every individual and treat colleagues and customers with professionalism, fairness and empathy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Obsession with Customers – We place customer outcomes at the centre of everything we do, striving to deliver meaningful value and exceptional experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountability – We take ownership of our actions, decisions and results, holding ourselves and each other to high standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rethink Tomorrow – We embrace innovation, challenge the status quo and continuously improve how we work to shape a better future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Joblogic Story&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Established in 1998,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic&lt;/strong&gt; is the UK’s #1 &lt;strong&gt;Field Service Management&lt;/strong&gt; (FSM) software platform. We are a global business with offices in the &lt;strong&gt;UK&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Pakistan&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Vietnam&lt;/strong&gt;. Since our management buy-out in 2013, we have grown from &lt;strong&gt;~£500K &lt;/strong&gt;ARR to &lt;strong&gt;~£35M+ &lt;/strong&gt;ARR and expanded our team from 11 to 500+ people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recently, we secured a strategic growth investment from &lt;strong&gt;Vista Equity Partners &lt;/strong&gt;— a global technology investor specialising in enterprise software. This investment includes over &lt;strong&gt;£100&lt;/strong&gt; million in new primary capital and will fuel our next phase of growth by accelerating our &lt;strong&gt;AI-first roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;, expanding our platform into CAFM (Computer-Aided Facilities Management) capabilities, and supporting our expansion across Europe and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With &lt;strong&gt;Vista’s &lt;/strong&gt;backing, we’re transforming from a successful UK business into a global scaling SaaS rocket ship, and we’d love for you to join us on our journey to &lt;strong&gt;£100M &lt;/strong&gt;ARR across international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic &lt;/strong&gt;provides software to service contractors who install and maintain the built environment. Our platform helps businesses streamline operations, improve profitability, ensure compliance, and achieve rapid growth. With over &lt;strong&gt;100,000&lt;/strong&gt; users across industries including HVAC, plumbing, electrical maintenance, facilities management, and building fabric maintenance, we are entering a new era of intelligent automation, predictive maintenance, and data-driven decision-making for service firms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about_the_role_0&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Product Manager with strong experience in Field Service Management (FSM), Facility Management, or operational workflow-driven SaaS products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager at Joblogic, you will play a key role in shaping the future of our platform by deeply understanding how service contractors operate and translating complex operational workflows into intuitive product solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with engineering, UX, customer-facing teams, and customers themselves to identify real-world operational challenges and build solutions that simplify the daily work of engineers, planners, helpdesk teams, and operations managers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who enjoys solving real operational problems, working closely with users, and building workflow-driven B2B SaaS products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what_your_main_focus_will_be_1&quot;&gt;What your main focus will be&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead discovery with customers across&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;field service and facilities management operations&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understand and map operational workflows including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reactive maintenance jobs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Planned Preventative Maintenance (PPM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scheduling and dispatch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Field engineer mobile workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Asset lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quote → job → invoicing journeys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You will be expected to:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex operational problems into clear product requirements and solution design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with UX designers to create intuitive workflows and product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and prioritise roadmap initiatives aligned with product strategy and customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering teams to ensure solutions are practical, scalable, and deliver real operational impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate product ideas through customer interviews, field research, and prototype testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor product adoption, workflow performance, and user behaviour to continuously improve features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with internal teams including Sales, Customer Success, and Support to ensure successful feature adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what_you_bring_2&quot;&gt;What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience as a Product Manager within B2B SaaS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Field Service Management, Facilities Management, or operational workflow-based software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating real-world operational processes into clear product logic and requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong discovery skills and ability to conduct customer interviews and uncover real problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating closely with UX designers and engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to manage stakeholders and communicate product strategy clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured thinking and ability to break down complex workflows into scalable product solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in fast-moving product environments with multiple priorities and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;nice_to_have_points_3&quot;&gt;Nice-to-have points&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;CAFM / FSM / CMMS software platforms&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;scheduling engines or optimisation logic&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;mobile-first workflows for frontline users&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;API-driven platforms and system integrations&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;data-driven operational analytics and reporting systems&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;remuneration_package_and_benefits_4&quot;&gt;Remuneration package and benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary based on experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work within a global SaaS product company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career progression opportunities as Joblogic continues to scale internationally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, product-focused and innovative working environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular company events and team activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development through Joblogic Academy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to internal training and product leadership mentoring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Joblogic Story&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Established in 1998,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic&lt;/strong&gt; is the UK’s #1 &lt;strong&gt;Field Service Management&lt;/strong&gt; (FSM) software platform. We are a global business with offices in the &lt;strong&gt;UK&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Pakistan&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Vietnam&lt;/strong&gt;. Since our management buy-out in 2013, we have grown from &lt;strong&gt;~£500K &lt;/strong&gt;ARR to &lt;strong&gt;~£35M+ &lt;/strong&gt;ARR and expanded our team from 11 to 500+ people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recently, we secured a strategic growth investment from &lt;strong&gt;Vista Equity Partners &lt;/strong&gt;— a global technology investor specialising in enterprise software. This investment includes over &lt;strong&gt;£100&lt;/strong&gt; million in new primary capital and will fuel our next phase of growth by accelerating our &lt;strong&gt;AI-first roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;, expanding our platform into CAFM (Computer-Aided Facilities Management) capabilities, and supporting our expansion across Europe and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With &lt;strong&gt;Vista’s &lt;/strong&gt;backing, we’re transforming from a successful UK business into a global scaling SaaS rocket ship, and we’d love for you to join us on our journey to &lt;strong&gt;£100M &lt;/strong&gt;ARR across international markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joblogic &lt;/strong&gt;provides software to service contractors who install and maintain the built environment. Our platform helps businesses streamline operations, improve profitability, ensure compliance, and achieve rapid growth. With over &lt;strong&gt;100,000&lt;/strong&gt; users across industries including HVAC, plumbing, electrical maintenance, facilities management, and building fabric maintenance, we are entering a new era of intelligent automation, predictive maintenance, and data-driven decision-making for service firms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Software QA Automation Engineer is responsible for ensuring software quality through structured manual testing, with a focus on progressively increasing automated test coverage. This role involves validating features, user flows, edge cases, and overall system behavior, while also contributing to automation frameworks and CI/CD integration within an Agile environment. Experience with Test-Driven Development (TDD) and Behavior-Driven Development (BDD) is highly valued to detect defects early in the development cycle.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manual Testing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Execute thorough manual test cycles for features, user flows, edge cases, and regression.&lt;br&gt;• Design detailed test scenarios and test cases.&lt;br&gt;• Ensure test coverage across functional, regression, integration, performance, and UI layers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;• Build and maintain automated tests using tools like Selenium, Playwright, or Cypress.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Perform API testing and automate API test cases where applicable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Integrate automation into CI/CD pipelines.&lt;br&gt;• Ensure automated tests run reliably in CI/CD pipelines with proper reporting and failure analysis.&lt;br&gt;• Support TDD and BDD practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Process Support:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Work closely with developers, product managers, and DevOps teams. &lt;br&gt;• Contribute to QA process improvements and automation frameworks. &lt;br&gt;• Support release processes, identify risks, and provide actionable insights.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bug Management:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Identify, report, track, and verify bugs using Jira. &lt;br&gt;• Analyze test results to highlight potential risks.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; • Education: Bachelor’s in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or related field. &lt;br&gt;• Experience: 3 years in QA, including 2+ years in automated testing.&lt;br&gt;• Testing Skills: Strong manual testing, test case design, and SDLC/STLC understanding. &lt;br&gt;• Automation Tools: Selenium, Playwright, Cypress; ability to write/debug scripts in Java, JavaScript, or Python. &lt;br&gt;• Methodologies: Agile/Scrum, CI/CD, DevOps practices, TDD, BDD.&lt;br&gt;• Tools: Jira for bug tracking and sprint management; Git-based systems like Azure DevOps; Jenkins knowledge.&lt;br&gt;• Soft Skills: Analytical thinking, attention to detail, effective communication.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Nice to Have:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Self-starter with a passion for quality.&lt;br&gt;• Mobile testing or cross-browser testing experience.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to work effectively in cross-functional teams.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we Offer?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;br&gt;• Professional Environment: A collaborative and dynamic workplace. • Competitive Salary: Market-leading compensation. &lt;br&gt;• Comprehensive Benefits: Medical insurance (including family), OPD, provident fund.&lt;br&gt;• Work-Life Balance: Maximum 45 weekly hours (Monday-Friday), 29 annual leaves, capped&lt;br&gt;• sick &amp;amp; compassionate leaves.&lt;br&gt;• Perks: Gym facility, annual company trip, quarterly team activities.&lt;/p&gt;

